 ### [Feed-Forward Hierarchical Gaussian Diffusion](19615-feed-forward-hierarchical-gaussian-diffusion.md)
-HiGDiff is a feed-forward reconstruction method for computed tomography (CT) that predicts a set of 3D Gaussian primitives from degraded projections without per-scene optimization. It solves the problem of sparse-view, low-dose, or limited-angle CT reconstruction by using two explicit Gaussian banks (structure and detail) initialized from anatomical cues and refined via a sequential structure-to-detail diffusion hierarchy. It differs from single-bank Gaussian reconstruction by maintaining separate banks for global attenuation geometry and residual detail.
